# Line endings are pinned here so they do not depend on each developer's
# global Git config. Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, which
# checks text files out as CRLF and then warns on every `git add` that "LF
# will be replaced by CRLF". Setting eol=lf explicitly overrides autocrlf for
# this repository, so Windows, macOS, and the Linux/musl CI build all see
# byte-identical files and the warning stops.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Called through a POSIX shell; CRLF would break the shebang line.
*.sh text eol=lf
# PowerShell reads LF fine on Windows, listed for symmetry with make.sh.
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# Never run EOL conversion or diff these as text.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.exe binary
